 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "The middle prayer glossed as Asr (Al-Muyassar; the view of most scholars). STAGING v4: 238-239: believers praying on a journey (the camel: riding, As-Sa'di); on «فرجالا/ركبانا» they walk, then pray in full when safe. No enemy is drawn. 240-242: a family at home (people group), the man of the house (heir/guardian) hands them their provision on «متاعا» and «متاع»; no widow or divorcee is singled out; the husband's death is not shown."
